00:08:32.534 --> 00:08:35.000
And we had Ray in one of them,

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.734
and at the end of it,
he had a really good time

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:39.200
and he was like, "You know,

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.634
I never would,
you know, ever..."

00:08:41.634 --> 00:08:43.367
It's a horrible impression.
-No.

00:08:43.367 --> 00:08:44.534
No, you got to save this
for Saturday.

00:08:44.534 --> 00:08:45.701
-It's not fair.

00:08:45.701 --> 00:08:46.901
It's like doing,
like, a Walken or whatever.

00:08:46.901 --> 00:08:48.467
It's just like everybody
has a Ray Romano.

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:49.801
He was so sweet,
he had a good time,

00:08:49.801 --> 00:08:51.801
and he was like, "You know,
I love this episode.

00:08:51.801 --> 00:08:53.234
I love being in one."

00:08:53.234 --> 00:08:57.767
He goes, "It'd be pretty crazy
if I showed up in another."

00:08:57.767 --> 00:08:59.467
And I was like, "Do you
wanna --" Yeah, I was like,

00:08:59.467 --> 00:09:00.601
"I'll do it right now."

00:09:00.601 --> 00:09:01.734
He's like, "Eh, you know,
it's not my show.

00:09:01.734 --> 00:09:03.434
I'm just, like, saying..."

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:04.701
-And then he did.
He did three of them.

00:09:04.701 --> 00:09:06.334
He's the man.
He's the coolest guy.

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:07.801
Also, check out his movie --
"Somewhere in Queens"

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:08.901
just came out.

00:09:08.901 --> 00:09:10.434
It's murdering.
-It's actually fantastic.

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:12.067
It's great, yeah.
-It's so incredible.

00:09:12.067 --> 00:09:13.300
I have one funny "Pesch"
story for you, though.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.601
-Yeah, tell me.

00:09:14.601 --> 00:09:16.400
-Because Pesch doesn't --
I'm very private about him,

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.734
because he's
a sweet, private man.

00:09:17.734 --> 00:09:21.100
But there's one thing
I want everybody to know that.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.000
So, you know, he's very nice.
If you're nice, he's nice.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.200
-Yeah, of course.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.033
-But, you know,
he tries to keep to himself,

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:30.100
unless you're a kid and you
recognize him from "Home Alone."

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.901
And this is something he did.

00:09:31.901 --> 00:09:34.267
And, obviously, I am a big
"Home Alone" guy, too,

00:09:34.267 --> 00:09:36.701
so I got to see this.

00:09:36.701 --> 00:09:40.834
If there was ever a kid that
noticed him as his character,

00:09:40.834 --> 00:09:42.567
he would go up to them
and he would go,

00:09:42.567 --> 00:09:44.901
"Listen, kid."

00:09:44.901 --> 00:09:48.434
He goes, "You better be good
to your parents this Christmas,

00:09:48.434 --> 00:09:50.634
because if you don't,
me and my pal Marv

00:09:50.634 --> 00:09:52.868
are going to come find you."

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:53.901
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:53.901 --> 00:09:55.734
-Love you, Joe Pesci!
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:09:55.734 --> 00:09:57.634
And then -- Yeah.

00:09:57.634 --> 00:09:59.734
And then the kid would
be like, "Oh, my God."

00:09:59.734 --> 00:10:01.267
And then he would
look back at me and go.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.167
That's Pesch, yeah.
-That's Pesch right there.

00:10:05.167 --> 00:10:06.400
